# Dual Deployment Architecture (Permanent — Critical)

## Law

**One codebase. Two deployment editions. Never two products.**

| Edition | `APP_EDITION` | Who hosts | Who is the paying customer |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Self-hosted / On-prem | `SELF_HOSTED` | Buyer’s VPS/server | You sell a **license/install** to one organization |
| SaaS / Shared platform | `SAAS` | Your infrastructure | End users buy **subscriptions** on your platform |

Same Core: Identity, Business tenancy, Entitlements, Document Engine, PDF, modules.

## Non-negotiable design

1. Build **Tenant-ready from day one** (`businessId` + guards). Do **not** build a single-company app and “add SaaS later”.
2. Do **not** fork repos (`vdb-saas` vs `vdb-onprem`). Editions are **config + optional packages**, not copy-paste.
3. `SELF_HOSTED` still uses Business isolation (org may have many businesses). Difference is **platform tenancy / billing owner**, not absence of `businessId`.
4. Default deploy target for both editions: **Docker / VPS** with NestJS + Next.js + PostgreSQL + Redis + MongoDB. Shared PHP cPanel is **not** the primary target.

## Edition behavior matrix

| Concern | `SELF_HOSTED` | `SAAS` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Platform multi-customer | One org owns the install (optional single root Organization) | Many independent customers on one install |
| Business subscriptions | Internal plans/modules still apply for feature gates | Same; payment to platform owner (you) |
| Software license | Env/license key / contract activation for the install | N/A (you operate the platform) |
| Branding | Customer brand; optional hide “Powered by” | Your brand or white-label tier |
| SMS / payment keys | Customer’s providers in `.env` | Your providers (or per-tenant overrides later) |
| Signup | Often invite-only / admin-created users | Public OTP signup |
| Trial 7-day first Business | Configurable; usually ON for SaaS UX, optional for on-prem | ON by default |

## Implementation requirements

- Central config: `APP_EDITION=SELF_HOSTED|SAAS` (and related flags). No scattered `if (saas)` without an Edition/Config service.
- Billing adapters: `PlatformBilling` vs `LicenseGate` behind one Entitlement interface where possible.
- Installer path for on-prem: `.env.example`, migrations, queue worker, storage, docs in `docs/deploy/`.
- SaaS path: same artifact; different env + domain + backup strategy.
- Features that only make sense on SaaS (public marketplace, cross-customer **platform admin**) must be edition-gated — never break self-hosted builds. See `24-saas-platform-admin.mdc`.

## Forbidden

- Separate divergent codebases for the two sales motions.
- Removing `businessId` in self-hosted “to simplify”.
- Hardcoding your SaaS payment gateway into the only billing path with no adapter.
- Assuming shared cPanel/PHP hosting is the primary on-prem target.
